  {
    "source": "\"A few steps more, and our breaths were literally snatched from us by what we saw; so literally that Thornton, the psychic investigator, actually fainted in the arms of the dazed man who stood behind him. Norrys, his plump face utterly white and flabby, simply cried out inarticulately; whilst I think that what I did was to gasp or hiss, and cover my eyes. The man behind me - the only one of the party older than I - croaked the hackneyed \"My God!\" in the most cracked voice I ever heard. Of seven cultivated men, only Sir William Brinton retained his composure; a thing the more to his credit because he led the party and must have seen the sight first.\"-H.P. Lovecraft, \"Rats in the Walls\"",
    "target": "“再往前走几步，我们看到的景象几乎夺走了我们的呼吸；说是几乎夺走，因为那位通灵调查员桑顿竟真的昏倒在身后那名惊愕男子的怀里。诺里斯那张圆润的脸苍白而松弛，只会含糊地喊叫；我想我则是倒抽一口气，或是发出嘶声，并捂住双眼。我身后的那个人——一行人中唯一年长于我的——用我听过最嘶哑的声音，干巴巴地喊出那句陈词滥调：“天哪！”七位受过良好教育的男子中，只有威廉·布林顿爵士保持了镇定；这更值得称赞，因为他是队伍的领头人，也必定是第一个看到那景象的人。”——H·P·洛夫克רא夫特，《墙中之鼠》",
    "locations": [
      "installed_files/manual.txt:206"
    ],
    "kind": "ui"
  },
  {
    "source": "\"There flapped rhythmically a horde of tame, trained, hybrid winged things... not altogether crows, nor moles, nor buzzards, nor ants, nor decomposed human beings, but something I cannot and must not recall.\"-H.P. Lovecraft, \"The Festival\".",
    "target": "“一大群驯养、训练有素的杂交飞翼生物有节奏地拍打着翅膀……它们既不全是乌鸦，也不是鼹鼠、秃鹫、蚂蚁或腐烂的人类尸体，而是某种我不能、也不该回忆的东西。”——H·P·洛夫克רא夫特，《节日》",
    "locations": [
      "installed_files/data/monsters.xml:/monsters/monster[@id=MON_BYAKHEE]/text/description"
    ],
    "kind": "ui"
  }
]